You are given the complete list of groups in one fictional universe at a
single fixed point in time, with their member lists.

List pairs of groups where one group is organizationally part of the
other — a subdivision, class, squad, department, or division that belongs
to the larger group as an institution, not just an overlap in membership.

Definition: report (child, parent) — the smaller, contained group first,
the larger, containing group second. The child answers to, operates under,
or is officially a division of the parent. This is structural/institutional
membership, not an alliance or a rivalry — judge by organizational fact,
not by whether the two groups get along.
Test: would a member of the child group, if asked "what are you part of,
organizationally," name the parent group as the immediate answer?
Include: a class within a school, a squad or team within a larger force or
organization, a department within a company, a branch within a larger
faction, a family that operates as a formal sub-unit of a larger
institution the story treats as its own group.
ANTI: two groups whose members simply overlap by a few individuals are not
part_of — that is shared membership between peers, not hierarchy. Two
groups on the same side of a conflict are not part_of each other unless one
is genuinely a subdivision of the other's own structure. Do not report a
pair twice in both directions and do not report a group as part of itself.
Everything not listed is undefined. Listing nothing is a legal answer.
Use group names exactly as given.

Output JSON only:
{"pairs": [["<child>", "<parent>"], ...]}
